            "created_at": "2025-09-03T23:14:02.474188+00:00",
            "notes": "[Multiball](item_5d0e4135-f4e1-42fb-991a-417643064560) is a cornerstone of an orb debuff build. Again, we take this in round 2 because [Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb) is just more versatile and without the debuffs or ability power online, it has reduced effectiveness in round 1. \n\nSell off [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf). \n\nOur first debuff is [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505). The healing debuff will make enemy kills easier and also starve the enemy supports of healing points. If you're not concerned with the healing and/or are more concerned with mobile enemies, you can pick up [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) instead. It's more expensive, but also comes with bonus health. \n\nIf you have extra cash, either get [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6) for the straight ability power or [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) is an affordable way to get ability power and cooldown reduction.\n\nUse up the rest of your cash to continue building ability power unless you feel like you need more survivability. Keep [Armored Vest](item_358361e2-59be-4c81-b221-8a87f37809e6) or look for other items like [Vitality Amplifier](item_6b52b1c9-a924-4a93-8545-a1c205cf6927) or [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0).",
